{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design", "label": "Platform-Neutral Config-File References (Phase B) Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_instructions_file_terminology", "label": "Generic 'Instructions File' Terminology", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plugin runs on multiple harnesses that each read their own per-platform instruction file (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md); where a skill names CLAUDE.md as if it were the only file, that is a Claude-Code-centric assumption that does not hold on Codex, Gemini CLI, or OpenCode, so skills should use a generic term and let the platform-tools reference docs name each platform's preferred file."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_rule1_conventions_location", "label": "Rule 1: Conventions Location to 'your instructions file'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces 'Project-specific conventions (put in CLAUDE.md)' in writing-skills/SKILL.md with 'put in your instructions file' \u2014 a generic phrase rather than picking one filename, because different harnesses read different files and the platform-tools reference docs are the right place to name each platform's preferred file."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_rule2_violation_parenthetical", "label": "Rule 2: 'Instruction-File Violation' Parenthetical", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces '(explicit CLAUDE.md violation)' in receiving-code-review/SKILL.md with '(explicit instruction-file violation)' \u2014 the parenthetical signals the phrase actively violates rules many users put in their instruction files, and 'instruction file' is the natural cross-platform term covering AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md collectively without picking one filename or softening to 'common'."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_instructions_file_terminology", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_rule1_conventions_location", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_platform_neutral_config_refs_design_rule2_violation_parenthetical", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-05-platform-neutral-config-refs-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_05_pla